-# 🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2
+# USDC Payouts
 
-<h4 align="center">
-  <a href="https://docs.scaffoldeth.io">Documentation</a> |
-  <a href="https://scaffoldeth.io">Website</a>
-</h4>
+Send USDC payouts to teammates and contributors on Base.
 
-🧪 An open-source, up-to-date toolkit for building decentralized applications (dapps) on the Ethereum blockchain. It's designed to make it easier for developers to create and deploy smart contracts and build user interfaces that interact with those contracts.
+The `Payouts` contract pulls USDC from the sender via `transferFrom` and forwards it straight to the
+recipient, emitting a `Paid` event with an optional memo so the payout history is public and
+auditable. The frontend at `/payouts` handles the approve → pay flow and renders the feed.
 
-> [!NOTE]
-> 🤖 Scaffold-ETH 2 is AI-ready! It has everything agents need to build on Ethereum. Check `.agents/`, `.claude/`, `.opencode` or `.cursor/` for more info.
-
-⚙️ Built using NextJS, RainbowKit, Hardhat, Wagmi, Viem, and Typescript.
-
-- ✅ **Contract Hot Reload**: Your frontend auto-adapts to your smart contract as you edit it.
-- 🪝 **[Custom hooks](https://docs.scaffoldeth.io/hooks/)**: Collection of React hooks wrapper around [wagmi](https://wagmi.sh/) to simplify interactions with smart contracts with typescript autocompletion.
-- 🧱 [**Components**](https://docs.scaffoldeth.io/components/): Collection of common web3 components to quickly build your frontend.
-- 🔥 **Burner Wallet & Local Faucet**: Quickly test your application with a burner wallet and local faucet.
-- 🔐 **Integration with Wallet Providers**: Connect to different wallet providers and interact with the Ethereum network.
-
-![Debug Contracts tab](https://github.com/scaffold-eth/scaffold-eth-2/assets/55535804/b237af0c-5027-4849-a5c1-2e31495cccb1)
+Built on [Scaffold-ETH 2](https://scaffoldeth.io) (Hardhat flavor): NextJS, RainbowKit, Wagmi, Viem,
+TypeScript.
 
 ## Requirements
 
-Before you begin, you need to install the following tools:
-
 - [Node (>= v20.18.3)](https://nodejs.org/en/download/)
 - Yarn ([v1](https://classic.yarnpkg.com/en/docs/install/) or [v2+](https://yarnpkg.com/getting-started/install))
 - [Git](https://git-scm.com/downloads)
 
-## Quickstart
+## Layout
 
-To get started with Scaffold-ETH 2, follow the steps below:
+- `packages/hardhat/contracts/Payouts.sol` — the payouts contract
+- `packages/hardhat/deploy/00_deploy_payouts.ts` — deploy script, points the contract at Base USDC
+- `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx` — the payouts UI
+- `packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts` — USDC (not deployed by us, so it lives here and
+  survives `yarn deploy`, which regenerates `deployedContracts.ts`)
+- `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts` — target network, polling interval, RPC overrides
 
-1. Install dependencies if it was skipped in CLI:
+## Local development
 
 ```
-cd my-dapp-example
 yarn install
+yarn chain     # terminal 1: local Hardhat network
+yarn deploy    # terminal 2: deploy Payouts
+yarn start     # terminal 3: NextJS app on http://localhost:3000
 ```
 
-2. Run a local network in the first terminal:
+Note that `scaffold.config.ts` targets Base mainnet. To develop against the local chain, add
+`chains.hardhat` to `targetNetworks` and deploy a USDC mock.
 
-```
-yarn chain
-```
+Run contract tests with `yarn hardhat:test`.
 
-This command starts a local Ethereum network using Hardhat. The network runs on your local machine and can be used for testing and development. You can customize the network configuration in `packages/hardhat/hardhat.config.ts`.
+## Environment
 
-3. On a second terminal, deploy the test contract:
+Copy `packages/nextjs/.env.example` to `packages/nextjs/.env.local` and fill in:
 
-```
-yarn deploy
-```
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL` — dedicated Base RPC. **Required in production**; without it the app
+  falls back to a shared public endpoint and gets rate limited.
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` — used for the mainnet fallback (ENS, ETH price).
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID` — get your own at https://cloud.walletconnect.com.
 
-This command deploys a test smart contract to the local network. The contract is located in `packages/hardhat/contracts` and can be modified to suit your needs. The `yarn deploy` command uses the deploy script located in `packages/hardhat/deploy` to deploy the contract to the network. You can also customize the deploy script.
+The same variables must be set in the host (Vercel) environment for the deployed app.
 
-4. On a third terminal, start your NextJS app:
+For contract deploys and verification, `packages/hardhat/.env` needs `ALCHEMY_API_KEY` and
+`ETHERSCAN_API_KEY`, plus a deployer account (`yarn generate` or `yarn account:import`).
+
+## Deploying
 
 ```
-yarn start
+yarn deploy --network base
+yarn verify --network base   # verify on Basescan
+yarn vercel:yolo --prod      # frontend
 ```
-
-Visit your app on: `http://localhost:3000`. You can interact with your smart contract using the `Debug Contracts` page. You can tweak the app config in `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts`.
-
-Run smart contract test with `yarn hardhat:test`
-
-- Edit your smart contracts in `packages/hardhat/contracts`
-- Edit your frontend homepage at `packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx`. For guidance on [routing](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/routing/defining-routes) and configuring [pages/layouts](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/routing/pages-and-layouts) checkout the Next.js documentation.
-- Edit your deployment scripts in `packages/hardhat/deploy`
-
